{"added":{"value":"2026-09-24"},"brand":{"value":"Dayton Audio"},"curves":{"frequency_response":{"origin":"manufacturer_product_page","value":{"data_format":"frd","local_path":"response_data/response.frd","type":"FILE"}},"impedance":{"origin":"manufacturer_product_page","value":{"data_format":"zma","local_path":"response_data/response.zma","type":"FILE"}}},"data_sources":{"value":{"manufacturer_datasheet":"https://daytonaudio.com/images/resources/295-730--dayton-audio-ss10-22-specification-sheet.pdf","manufacturer_product_page":"https://daytonaudio.com/product/2127/ss10-22-10-signature-series-dvc-subwoofer-2-ohms-per-coil"}},"description":{"value":"The Dayton Audio SS10-22 Signature Series 10\" Subwoofer is engineered for powerful, controlled bass from compact enclosures. With its rigid anodized aluminum cone, dual-spider suspension, and a massive triple-stacked motor structure, the SS10-22 maintains pistonic accuracy and low distortion even at extreme excursion. A 2.5\" 4-layer copper voice coil on a vented aluminum former ensures excellent thermal handling, allowing the driver to manage up to 700 watts RMS without compression. Designed for DSP-assisted sealed enclosures or compact vented/passive radiator systems, the SS10-22 is equally at home in home theater, hi-fi listening rooms, or car audio installations where deep bass performance in a smaller footprint is required. Product Highlights Aluminum shorting sleeve, ring, and pole cap ensure linear inductance and ultra-low distortion Rigid anodized aluminum cone with indexed edge for pistonic accuracy and reduced resonance 2.5\" 4-layer copper voice coil on a vented aluminum former for superior power handling and cooling Massive triple-stacked magnet assembly delivers exceptional strength and symmetry at high excursion Extensive venting through cone, pole piece, spider, and gap minimizes thermal buildup and compression Dual spider suspension with stitched tinsel leads for precise pistonic motion and enhanced durab